        "x2": 1935.0,
        "y2": 1988.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.7834978103637695,
      "reading_order": 15,
      "text": "10. $E_2 = \\frac{-13.6 \\times Z^2}{n^2}$\n\n$\\therefore -x = \\frac{-13.6 \\times Z^2}{4}$\n\n$\\therefore Z^2 = \\frac{4x}{13.6}$\n\n$\\therefore Z = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{13.6}}$\n\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
